# Sample requests for the API. Start it first, either way:
#   fastapi dev app/main.py             (on your computer)
#   docker compose up --build           (in Docker)
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above a request.
# JetBrains IDEs run this file as is.

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### Is the API up? Is the model loaded?
GET {{base}}/health

### How was the model trained, how good is it, which features matter?
GET {{base}}/models

### Invent a character: a young Stark knight with 3 dead relatives
POST {{base}}/got/predict
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ser Sovann of Phnom Penh",
  "male": true,
  "house": "stark",
  "culture": "northmen",
  "title": "knight",
  "noble": true,
  "married": false,
  "age": 21,
  "dead_relatives": 3,
  "popularity": 0.6,
  "books": [1, 2, 3]
}

### A quiet maester who only shows up in book 4 (leave out what you don't know)
POST {{base}}/got/predict
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Maester Nobody",
  "title": "maester",
  "books": [4]
}

### Several characters in one call
POST {{base}}/got/predict/batch
Content-Type: application/json

[
  {"name": "Doomed Prince", "house": "targaryen", "title": "royalty", "noble": true,
   "dead_relatives": 8, "popularity": 0.9, "age": 30, "books": [1]},
  {"name": "Lucky Steward", "house": "night's watch", "title": "office", "books": [4, 5]}
]

### Real characters: what the model says vs. what the books say
GET {{base}}/got/characters?search=Stark&limit=5

### Is Jon Snow safe?
GET {{base}}/got/characters?search=Jon Snow

### Invalid input -> 422 (book 6 is not out, "House Stark" is not a valid value, unknown field)
POST {{base}}/got/predict
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "house": "House Stark",
  "books": [6],
  "has_dragons": true
}
